WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.500
TSM L one. Governed technician intelligence, running in the real application.

2
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.900
The problem: ticket context is scattered, and every technician pieces it together differently.

3
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:22.900
TSM classifies the ticket, sets the next action, and shows closure blocked until the evidence is in.

4
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:30.000
The assistant recommends Return to Inventory, labelled as a draft. It recommends. It does not act.

5
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Nothing changes until the technician authorizes it.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The action is confirmed and recorded.

7
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Closure stays blocked until the location is verified. The ticket cannot close on incomplete evidence.

8
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.000
A software request gets different required steps, automatically.

9
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Leadership sees the same work in the executive view.

10
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:09.300
Understand, prepare, verify, a technician confirms, and the result is recorded. The aim: consistent work, and evidence you can audit.

